Well, this is not really on good authority or anything, since I've yet to try
this little trick, but I'm told that a potion of paralysis when tossed at the
wizard will mess him up.

I really should try these scams out myself before posting them   ;^).

Stormbringer is definitely a good weapon to use against him too.

The nature of the game, though, is that underestimating monsters is fatal.
But once you surpass a certain level in your intrinsics and equipment even
the wizard will seem like a wimp.

Now, to me it seems like that the kind of power that a high-level character
is throwing around in a fight with the wizard should be earth-shaking.  Your
blows should knock him through walls, and his should do the same to you.
There should be blinding flashes of light, deafening, thunderous crashes
from the power of the blows, and fear should be struck in the hearts of
all the feebler creatures who witness this incredible display of power.
Both you and the wizard would become blind (from the flashes) and deaf
(from the crashes) - (hey - that rhymes), but by now you have telepathy
I'm sure, so who's complaining?

I mean, we're talking about the power to dispatch huge creatures with a
single blow!  Witnessing this would be an experience, and the game-generated
chatter should reflect a battle of titanic proportions.

Now, *that* would be a fight to remember!

(Of course, you would have to be powerful enough for these "special effects"
to kick in.  Otherwise the wizard would just smash the stuffings out of you
and laugh in your face just before snuffing out your whimpering life.)
